{
	"name": "Insulting Banner",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/sundries/flags/banner-flag-white.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Raising your banner high and calling out to the heavens, you attempt to invoke a blessing upon your allies, but you are met with merciless laughter. While this banner looks like a @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-adventuring-gear.Item.8Tq6cGDXxvxsiMzW]{Blessed Banner} it is in fact a cursed item. When not in combat this banner functions like a Blessed Banner, however, if you attempt to use it while engaged in battle it instead casts @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-spells.Item.ohrkuqnbaeutcwox]{Vicious Mockery} on all creatures within 10ft, including you, as a 5th level Bard dealing 2d6 psychic damage and causing your next attack roll to have disadvantage. A Wisdom saving throw DC 16 negates the effect.</p>",
